description: Terms and conditions for one-off IT Surgery bookings, including the booking fee, no fix no fee, your right to cancel, and how we look after your data.
---

<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">

    <p class="lead">
      These are the terms for a <strong>one-off job</strong> — a repair, a
      setup, a visit or a remote session. If you are on one of our
      <a href="/support-plans/">support plans</a>, the
      <a href="/plan-terms/">support plan terms</a> apply to that instead.
      They are written to be read, not to catch you out. If anything is
      unclear, <a href="https://wa.me/{{ site.whatsapp }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">message us on WhatsApp<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
      or email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> and we
      will explain it before you book.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Who you are contracting with</h2>
    <p>
      IT Surgery is a trading name of {{ site.legalName }}, a company
      registered in England and Wales (company number {{ site.companyNumber }}),
      VAT registration number {{ site.vatNumber }}. Registered office:
      {{ site.address.street }}, {{ site.address.locality }},
      {{ site.address.town }}, {{ site.address.postcode }}.
      Contact: <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Booking fee</h2>
    <p>
      Holding a slot means turning someone else away, and travelling to a job
      that isn't there costs us the afternoon. The fee keeps bookings genuine.
    </p>
    <ul class="ticks wide">
      <li>We ask for a <strong>£{{ site.bookingFee }} booking fee</strong> to reserve your appointment.</li>
      <li>It comes off your first hour — it is not an extra charge.</li>
      <li><strong>No fix, no fee.</strong> If we cannot solve the problem, we refund the booking fee in full and you pay nothing.</li>
      <li>If we can solve it but you decide not to go ahead once we have told you what is involved, we keep the booking fee for the time spent diagnosing.</li>
      <li><strong>We never see or store your card details.</strong> Your invoice is raised in Xero, our accounting system, and the card payment itself is handled by Stripe.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. What it costs</h2>
    <ul class="ticks wide">
      <li>Home customers: <strong>£{{ site.hourlyRate }} an hour {{ site.vatIncLabel }}</strong>.</li>
      <li>Business customers: <strong>£{{ site.businessHourlyRate }} an hour {{ site.vatExLabel }}</strong>.</li>
      <li>We charge for the time we actually spend, rounded to the nearest fifteen minutes after the first hour.</li>
      <li>Parts, replacement hardware and software licences are extra. We will always tell you the price and get your agreement before buying anything.</li>
      <li>If a job is going to take longer than we expected, we stop and tell you before carrying on.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Where we work</h2>
    <p>
      We cover {{ site.areas | join(", ") }} and the surrounding Vale of
      Glamorgan for on-site visits. Remote support is available anywhere in the
      UK. If you are outside our area, ask — we will tell you straight away
      rather than waste your time.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Remote sessions.</strong> Many problems can be sorted without
      anyone travelling. You will get a link to join at the time you booked,
      and you stay at the computer throughout — you can see everything we do,
      and you can end the session at any moment, for any reason. We will ask
      before changing anything. Please close online banking and anything else
      private before we start.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Changing or cancelling an appointment</h2>
    <ul class="ticks wide">
      <li>Change or cancel with <strong>24 hours' notice</strong> or more and we refund the booking fee in full, or move it to your new appointment.</li>
      <li>Less than 24 hours, or if nobody is there when we arrive, we keep the booking fee to cover the reserved time.</li>
      <li>If <em>we</em> have to change or cancel, you get the booking fee back in full, and we will do our best to offer you a slot that suits.</li>
      <li>Things happen — illness, family, emergencies. Tell us and we will be reasonable.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Your 14-day right to cancel (home customers)</h2>
    <p>
      If you are a consumer and you booked online, by message or over the
      phone, you have a legal right to cancel within <strong>14 days</strong>,
      for any reason, under the Consumer Contracts (Information, Cancellation
      and Additional Charges) Regulations 2013.
    </p>
    <ul class="ticks wide">
      <li>To cancel, just tell us — <a href="https://wa.me/{{ site.whatsapp }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a> or email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. A simple message is enough; you do not need to give a reason or use any particular form.</li>
      <li>We will refund everything you have paid within 14 days of being told.</li>
      <li><strong>If you want us to start sooner than that</strong>, you can ask us to — most people do, because a broken computer will not wait. You keep the right to cancel, but if we have already done work you will pay a fair amount for what we actually provided. We will tell you the figure before deducting anything.</li>
      <li>Once we have completely finished the job at your request within those 14 days, the right to cancel that job ends.</li>
      <li>This right does not apply to business customers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Backups and your data</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Please back up anything you cannot afford to lose before we start.</strong>
      We will always ask, and we will help you do it if you are not sure how.
    </p>
    <p>
      We take reasonable care with your equipment and your files. But repairs
      sometimes involve hardware that is already failing, and no engineer can
      guarantee data survives a failing disk. We are not responsible for data
      that was not backed up beforehand.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a job carries a real risk to your data, we will tell you before we
      touch anything, so you can decide.
    </p>
    <p>
      How we handle your personal information is set out in our
      <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Access, and what we need from you</h2>
    <ul class="ticks wide">
      <li>For a visit, someone aged 18 or over needs to be at home for the whole appointment.</li>
      <li>For a remote session, you need to be at the computer for the whole appointment, switched on and connected to the internet.</li>
      <li>We will need passwords for the devices we are working on. Never give us your online banking password — we will never ask for it.</li>
      <li>If we find something unsafe, unlicensed or unlawful, we will stop work and explain why.</li>
      <li>We can only work on equipment you own or have permission to have worked on.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Our responsibility to you</h2>
    <p>
      We will carry out our work with reasonable care and skill, as the law
      requires. If we get something wrong, we will put it right.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not exclude or limit our liability for death or personal injury
      caused by our negligence, for fraud, or for anything else that cannot
      lawfully be excluded. Otherwise, our liability for any one job is limited
      to the amount you paid us for that job. We are not liable for business
      losses such as lost profits or lost revenue — these terms are intended
      for households and small businesses, not for customers relying on us for
      business-critical continuity. If that is what you need, talk to us so we
      can quote for it properly.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing here affects your statutory rights. If you are a consumer, any
      term found to be unfair under the Consumer Rights Act 2015 will not apply.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Paying us</h2>
    <ul class="ticks wide">
      <li>Payment is due when the job is done, unless we have agreed otherwise in writing.</li>
      <li>Business customers may be invoiced on 14-day terms by arrangement.</li>
      <li>Any hardware we supply remains ours until it is paid for in full.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>11. Complaints</h2>
    <p>
      If something is not right, please tell us — <a href="https://wa.me/{{ site.whatsapp }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">message us on WhatsApp<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
      or email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. We would
      much rather hear about it and fix it. We will acknowledge your complaint
      within two working days and aim to resolve it within fourteen.
    </p>

    <h2>12. General</h2>
    <ul class="ticks wide">
      <li>These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and the courts of England and Wales have jurisdiction. If you live in Scotland or Northern Ireland you may bring proceedings in your own courts.</li>
      <li>If any part of these terms is found not to apply, the rest still stands.</li>
      <li>These terms were last updated in {{ site.privacyUpdated }}.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="cta-panel">
      <h2>Questions before you book?</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://wa.me/{{ site.whatsapp }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Message us on WhatsApp<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
        or <a href="/quote/">ask us to call you back</a>. We would rather spend
        ten minutes explaining than have you book something that is not right
        for you.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
